L highlights: Best plays, moments, touchdowns, more","description":"Check here for all of the top moments, TDs and analysis from games at the Broncos, Jets, Cowboys, Eagles and more.","published":"2026-11-23T04:50:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50562956/week-11-highlights-sunday-best-plays-touchdowns-2026","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"49ers make bold statement with blowout win over Vikings, keep NFC's No. 1 seed","description":"The 49ers used a late second-quarter burst to take control of Sunday's game in Mexico City and move to 9-1 on the season.","published":"2026-11-23T05:18:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50525677/49ers-beat-vikings-sunday-night-football-mexico-city-kittle","type":"Story","byline":"Nick Wagoner and Kevin Seifert","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Despite loss to Broncos, Fernando Mendoza settling in as Raiders' starting QB","description":"Fernando Mendoza, making his second start for the Raiders, had good and bad moments Sunday at Denver. He completed 18 of 37 passes for 267 yards and three touchdowns but was sacked five times and pressured 16 times, and threw a game-sealing pick-six.","published":"2026-11-23T05:08:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50569797/fernando-mendoza-settling-raiders-starting-quarterback","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Ryan McFadden","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ja'Quan McMillian hoping long-term future is in Denver after latest clutch play","description":"After Ja'Quan McMillian made a one-handed, 35-yard pick-six Sunday, his teammates surrounded him with a pay-the-man, count-that-money celebration.","published":"2026-11-23T04:46:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50569582/broncos-jaquan-mcmillian-comes-clutch-again","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jeff Legwold","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"RB Cam Skattebo backflips again after pledging to nix celebration","description":"Cam Skattebo's pledge to nix his trademark backflip didn't last long. Not even a week.","published":"2026-11-23T04:49:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50569390/rb-cam-skattebo-backflips-again-pledging-nix-celebration","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jordan Raanan","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Trevor Nowaske","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske","description":"American football player (born 1998)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:18Z","intro":"Trevor Nowaske (born November 7, 1998) is an American professional football linebacker for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Saginaw Valley State Cardinals. He signed with the Detroit Lions as an undrafted free agent in 2023.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"DETROIT LIONS\nOn May 12, 2023, the Detroit Lions signed Nowaske to a three-year, $2.695 million contract as an undrafted free agent. He was waived by Detroit on August 29, and was re-signed to the team's practice squad. On November 2, Nowaske was signed to the active roster. He was waived by the Lions on December 28.\n\nARIZONA CARDINALS\nOn December 29, 2023, Nowaske was claimed off waivers by the Arizona Cardinals. He was waived by the Cardinals on August 27, 2024.\n\nDETROIT LIONS (SECOND STINT)\nOn August 28, 2024, the Detroit Lions claimed Nowaske off waivers. On October 27 against the Tennessee Titans, Nowaske recorded his first interception off of Mason Rudolph.\nOn March 14, 2025, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions.\nOn March 16, 2026, Nowaske re-signed with the Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q121461325","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-03-13","text":"Signed DB Izien Christian and LB Trevor Nowaske to contracts."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/5144894","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/N/NowaTr00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/trevor-nowaske/169859","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/trevor-nowaske/11481","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevor_Nowaske"},"insights":["On the field for 30% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.4M is the 29th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2023 as an undrafted free agent."]}